                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Really digging this game so far, only getting off so soon because I have an early flight to catch tomorrow.  Right off the bat I [b]wouldn't recommend this to anyone who has photosensitive epilepsy[/b] as the graphics are EXTREMELY flashy with a multitude of colors.\n\nGameplay is [b]ridiculously[/b] fluid and it's very satisfying using the powerup provided once you've gathered enough star energy.  Using that bad boy inside of a survival stage and getting over a 1,000 hit count is such a good feeling even though I got my ass whooped shortly after.  The music is fitting.  The menus are minimal and are pretty right to the point.  I'm not great with identifying music but for anyone who enjoys D&B (I believe it to be) then this game's got a few jammy tracks of them.\n\nI haven't tried the co-op or multiplayer PvP, but I'm sure it's a grand time as the singleplayer.\n\nPros:\n-Works on Linux natively (Played on Pop!_US 17.10)\n-Great/Sensible keyboard controls (Haven't tested controller)\n-Fluid movement\n-Fluid shooting/combat\n-Good game sounds\n-Enjoyable music\n\nCons:\n-60 FPS Locked (not really a con, but I'm a numbers guy.  The more the better.)\n-On occasion the game will start to lag inside of a level.  Fixed by going back to main menu and continuing your stage.\n\nThis is just a small review, hope it gave enough information for anyone thinking about purchasing.",
